  "bach2": {"distribution":"one-type","specificityNote":"Specificity not established: no corpus medicine is aimed at it and the catalogues give it only the role biomarker; HPA finds the RNA group enriched, which says where the protein sits but not whether the tumour differs from normal tissue. HPA BACH2: RNA group enriched (bone marrow 7 nTPM, lymphoid tissue 16 nTPM); high antibody staining in 3 normal tissues; highest cancer staining lymphoma (3 of 12 high). Distribution: 1 cancer family in the corpus carries a prevalence row, label threshold or catalogue link for it (Leukaemia (all types)); Open Targets associates it with 2 specific cancer types at or above 0.5 (skin cancer, basal cell carcinoma); the corpus evidence decides and the Open Targets list is quoted for comparison. (No rule of scripts/fetch-target-specificity.ts fired.)","specificitySources":[{"label":"Human Protein Atlas BACH2 tissue","url":"https://www.proteinatlas.org/ENSG00000112182-BACH2/tissue","note":"RNA tissue and blood lineage specificity, normal tissue antibody staining (version 25.1, CC BY-SA 3.0)"},{"label":"Open Targets ENSG00000112182 associations","url":"https://platform.opentargets.org/target/ENSG00000112182/associations","note":"cancer associations at or above 0.5 (CC0)"}]},
